{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>All who go out of the gate of his city.</b> And further on it says regarding Sarah: לכל באי שער עירו. Rather, here, since everyone flees — because they needed to be circumcised against their will — it writes כל יוצאי: not one of them was permitted to go out until he was circumcised. But regarding Sarah, since everyone comes to do kindness for her, it writes לכל באי."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:07:19.220539099Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}